# Files excluded from `git archive`, which is what builds the Zenodo deposit.
#
# ZENODO_RECORD.json is a record OF the deposit, and it can only be written AFTER a version is
# published. Any copy inside an archive therefore describes the PREVIOUS version, by
# construction: v1.0.6's archive shipped a record describing v1.0.1, a different DOI and a
# different commit. Excluding it removes the possibility rather than correcting one instance.
# The published record on Zenodo is the authority for what a version contains.
source/ZENODO_RECORD.json export-ignore
